    description: "Residual of WI-majov (html <script src> resolution), found 2026-10-01 on dev af4e16964b. Same mechanism in the single-file-component analyzers: a component import of an EXISTING in-repo file points at a phantom external_symbol instead of the file's node, and the linker that recovers it mislabels the language.\n\nRepro fixture: src/App.svelte `<script>import Child from './Child.svelte';</script><Child />` with src/Child.svelte present; src/App.vue `import Kid from './Kid.vue'` + `<Kid />` with src/Kid.vue present. `hypergumbo run` gives:\n1. svelte: `svelte:src/App.svelte:1-1:file:file imports -> ./Child.svelte:<unknown>:0-0:./Child.svelte:external_symbol` (is_resolved False). svelte.py:237 `edge_dst = import_path` (raw string). WI-bufar covers this site's id-SLOT shape, not resolution onto the existing file.\n2. vue: `vue:src/App.vue:1-1:file:file imports -> vue:./Kid.vue:0-0:Kid:external_symbol` (is_resolved False). vue.py:561 builds the dst from the raw import path.\n3. js_ts also emits `javascript:src/App.svelte:1-1:file:file imports -> javascript:./Child.svelte:0-0:module:external_symbol` and the .vue equivalent: phantoms, because the js-module-linker resolves only JS/TS targets.\n4. vue-component-linker DOES add the resolved edge for both: `... imports -> vue:src/Kid.vue:1-1:file:file` (correct) and `svelte:src/App.svelte:1-1:file:file imports -> vue:src/Child.svelte:1-1:file:file`, which labels a .svelte file `vue`. That mints a vue-language file node for a Svelte file (vue_component.py ~200 `make_file_id(\"vue\", rel_path)` on any matched path).\n5. Each .svelte/.vue file has two file nodes, `javascript:src/App.svelte:...` and `svelte:src/App.svelte:...` (likewise vue). Whether that duplication is intended (two analyzers over one file) is not checked here; INV-movor's statement says one file-kind Symbol per path.\n\nSo each component import yields up to two phantom edges beside one real (sometimes mislabelled) edge. Fix direction, as for html in WI-majov: resolve a relative import path against the importing file's directory and point at the target's canonical file id with the target's own language, and keep a placeholder only when nothing resolves. Astro (astro.py:314, the same bare-path shape) was not repro'd.\n\nNot measured: corpus counts."  # 357d
